(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[8 1 "// Descriptors (PY5c; CPython's Objects/descrobject.c, funcobject.c's classmethod and staticmethod,"] [9 1 "// classobject.c's method, typeobject.c's super and slot wrappers): bound methods, functions as"] [10 1 "// descriptors, classmethod, staticmethod, property, __slots__' members, super, the slot wrappers"] [11 1 "// that show a built-in type's slots as methods, and the attributes of types, functions and methods."] [15 2 "// MethodWrapperType is method-wrapper (descrobject.c's _PyMethodWrapper_Type, queue 290): a slot wrapper bound to an"] [16 2 "// instance ((2).__pow__, object().__str__), a *Method whose Func is a *slotWrapper; inspect's _NonUserDefinedCallables"] [17 2 "// tell it from a Python bound method"] [19 2 "// ClassMethodDescrType is classmethod_descriptor (descrobject.c's PyClassMethodDescr_Type, queue 290): a built-in"] [20 2 "// type's class method as its class holds it (dict.__dict__['fromkeys']), a *ClassMethod not made by classmethod()"] [21 2 "// around a *Builtin"] [32 1 "// Method is a bound method: a function and the object it is bound to."] [44 1 "// ClassMethod and StaticMethod wrap a callable."] [46 12 "// made by classmethod(...), not a built-in type's"] [58 1 "// isDescr: c is a built-in type's classmethod_descriptor (a *Builtin not wrapped by classmethod())."] [74 1 "// Property is property(fget, fset, fdel, doc)."] [78 27 "// a subclass of property"] [88 1 "// Member is a __slots__ entry's descriptor."] [97 1 "// Super is super(type, obj)."] [106 1 "// slotWrapper is a built-in type's slot as a method (wrapper_descriptor)."] [115 1 "// mappingProxy is a type's __dict__ read only."] [118 11 "// the type whose __dict__ it is, or nil"] [119 11 "// the mapping, when it is no dict (mappingproxy(UserDict()))"] [122 1 "// proxied is the mapping behind p."] [146 1 "// newWrappers are the built-in types' __new__ objects, one each."] [154 1 "// slotWrappers keep one wrapper per type and name, so that int.__repr__ is int.__repr__ (enum compares"] [155 1 "// a class's methods with its data type's and object's; PY5e, part 2b)."] [158 1 "// slotWrapperFor is built-in type m's slot for the special method name, or nil."] [166 3 "// METH_COEXIST (queue 290): the method its type defines beside the slot, a method_descriptor"] [167 3 "// (frozenset.__contains__ bound is a builtin_function_or_method: keyword.iskeyword)"] [176 1 "// coexistMethods are the built-in types' METH_COEXIST methods (dict_methods', list_methods', set_methods' and"] [177 1 "// frozenset_methods' __getitem__ and __contains__): method descriptors where the other slots have slot wrappers."] [199 2 "// the number protocol's binary methods (__add__, __radd__, __iadd__ ...): the Binary, RBinary and InPlace"] [200 2 "// slots, NotImplemented when they do not apply (PY6h's REQUEST, queue 200: test_asyncio reads int.__add__)"] [225 6 "// wrap_ternaryfunc_r: the operands swapped, the modulus third"] [238 22 "// wrap_indexargfunc"] [249 4 "// object_str: tp_repr, never the type's own __str__ (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: a class with"] [250 4 "// __str__ = object.__str__, doctest's DocTestCase, recursed without end)"] [371 5 "// dict_subscript sees self's type: a subclass's d.__getitem__(k) calls its __missing__ as d[k] does"] [372 5 "// (queue 202: urllib.parse's _Quoter(safe).__getitem__ raised KeyError: test_http_cookies,"] [373 5 "// test_wsgiref's request_uri)"] [481 3 "// one object per type, so that object.__new__ is object.__new__ (enum's _find_new_ compares them;"] [482 3 "// PY5e, part 2b)"] [534 29 "// unicode__format__: an empty spec, a subclass's str()"] [568 1 "// hackCheck is hackcheck: m's __setattr__ called on self, whose built-in base nearest to its type overrides it"] [569 1 "// (object.__setattr__(str, ...) would jump over type's own)."] [579 22 "// of the built-in bases one can reach here, only type overrides tp_setattro"] [586 1 "// objectDir is object.__dir__: the instance's dictionary's keys and its class's attributes."] [633 3 "// object's wrappers are made on demand (slotWrapperFor), add_operators' names here"] [656 1 "// superArgs are super()'s zero arguments: the running function's first argument and its __class__ cell."] [694 2 "// supercheck: a proxy's __class__ (a class it pretends to be an instance of)"] [721 2 "// method_reduce (classobject.c): getattr(self, the function's name)"] [736 2 "// functions as descriptors, bound methods"] [743 2 "// types.MethodType(func, instance) (method_new)"] [769 2 "// method_descr_get: a bound method is not bound again (gh-113157)"] [808 2 "// slot wrappers"] [845 2 "// method-wrapper (descrobject.c's wrapper_call, wrapper_repr, wrapper_richcompare, wrapper_hash, wrapper_members,"] [846 2 "// wrapper_getsets, wrapper_reduce; queue 290): a slot wrapper bound to its instance, no __func__ and no"] [847 2 "// delegation to the wrapper's attributes; not bound again as an attribute of a class (no tp_descr_get)"] [887 2 "// classmethod_descriptor (descrobject.c's classmethod_get, classmethoddescr_call, method_repr, descr_reduce; queue"] [888 2 "// 290): bound to the class it is asked through (a builtin_function_or_method whose __self__ is the class), called"] [889 2 "// with the class first"] [954 2 "// classmethod, staticmethod (funcobject.c): a subclass's instance is an Instance around the Go value, so every"] [955 2 "// slot unwraps; __init__ copies the wrapped callable's attributes (functools_wraps) into the dict"] [981 19 "// a classmethod made by a program, not a built-in type's descriptor"] [1007 3 "// a built-in type's classmethod_descriptor: a builtin_function_or_method bound to the class (dict.fromkeys)"] [1065 3 "// descriptor_get_wrapped_attribute and its setter: the dict first, the callable's value kept there"] [1110 2 "// property"] [1242 2 "// __slots__' members"] [1323 2 "// super"] [1370 5 "// a built-in type's method, or a method descriptor in a heap type's dict (methodDescrs: _ast's AST,"] [1371 5 "// queue 202c: super().__init__ in a node class's subclass)"] [1399 53 "// a subclass of super: its type called"] [1421 2 "// mappingproxy"] [1423 2 "// mappingproxy(mapping), over a dict (PY6a: enum's __members__); other mappings are the data model's"] [1431 3 "// an exact dict by its storage; a dict subclass (OrderedDict) as the mapping it is, so its repr and its"] [1432 3 "// comparison are its own (mappingproxy_new keeps the object; queue 278: inspect's Signature.parameters)"] [1436 3 "// mappingproxy_check_mapping: PyMapping_Check, not a list or a tuple"] [1449 2 "// a built-in type's own slots' wrappers (ownSlots, registry.go) are in its __dict__ too (PY5e, part 2b)"] [1457 14 "// a built-in type's attribute descriptors (type.__dict__['__annotations__']: annotationlib)"] [1489 2 "// mappingproxy_richcompare: the mapping's own comparison (queue 202: mappingproxy({}) == {} was False; test_re's"] [1490 2 "// test_getattr compares a pattern's groupindex with a dict)"] [1515 2 "// mappingproxy_or: the mappings beneath, a proxy's unwrapped on either side"] [1591 33 "// one object, as a static type's: pickle's memo shares it"] [1600 3 "// type_set_module: the class's __firstlineno__ goes with its old module (queue 278: inspect.getsource of"] [1601 3 "// _py_abc's ABCMeta, renamed into abc, raises OSError)"] [1643 21 "// inside the first mro()"] [1693 2 "// type_get_text_signature: the signature in tp_doc, for the types that have one here (func_new's clinic doc)"] [1697 19 "// a C type's tp_doc signature (arbace/pyctypes, queue 270b)"] [1701 37 "// CPython's for a built-in type (queue 290), a heap type's from its __doc__"] [1709 33 "// type_mro: mro_implementation afresh, a metaclass's mro() builds on it"] [1743 3 "// recursive_issubclass's check_class"] [1768 1 "// checkSetSpecial is check_set_special_type_attr."] [1924 2 "// method_descriptor's members and getsets (descrobject.c's descr_members, method_getset; queue 286)"] [1955 45 "// a module's function's module (m_self; queue 290)"] [1958 2 "// __module__ is func.go's (PY6d's R5: the function's module), which this init's order let override this one"] [1961 1 "// excSlots are the __slots__ values of exceptions (an exception class's instances are *Exception, not"] [1962 1 "// *Instance): PY6a, by the integration's owner, for test_exceptions' slotted exception classes."] [1965 1 "// setTypeBases is type.__bases__'s setter (typeobject.c's type_set_bases; PY6b's request: typing.NamedTuple"] [1966 1 "// assigns a class's bases): a heap type's bases replaced by types of the same instance layout, its MRO and its"] [1967 1 "// subclasses' computed again and their slots refilled."] [1986 3 "// a reentrant mro() has not set base's MRO yet: its __base__ is asked too"] [2012 2 "// nothing more when a reentrant assignment replaced the bases"] [2031 1 "// newStaticBase is tp_new_wrapper's staticbase (REQUEST of PY6g for PY6-core: test_descr's test_bad_new): t, or"] [2032 1 "// the first base along __base__ whose __new__ is not a Python class's own (slot_tp_new)."] [2040 1 "// newOrigin is the built-in type whose __new__ t's tp_new is (inherited along __base__ from the first one"] [2041 1 "// that defines it), CPython's tp_new pointer compared."] [2055 1 "// newAliases: the built-in types whose own __new__ here is CPython's inherited one (defaultdict's is dict_new)"] [2058 1 "// isNewWrapper: v is a built-in type's __new__ (tp_new_wrapper); a class whose __new__ is one keeps the"] [2059 1 "// __new__ it inherits (update_one_slot's special case), so that class C(list): __new__ = object.__new__"] [2060 1 "// makes lists"] [2073 1 "// ExtTextSignatureHook is a C extension's type's __text_signature__ (the signature its tp_doc begins with), found false"] [2074 1 "// for a type that is not one (arbace/pyctypes, queue 270b)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[38 35] [161 29] [165 31] [193 37] [233 37] [237 34] [251 67] [262 63] [267 68] [272 67] [288 37] [305 37] [327 37]